# Character & Creature Anatomy Modeling (`character-creature-anatomy-modeling`)

Modeling organic humans, animals, and fantasy creatures requires adherence to biological anatomy and deformation-friendly quad topology. Meshes with bad edge loops collapse, pinch, and tear when animated or posed by game engine skeletal armatures.

This skill establishes anatomical benchmarks, quad loop flows, and automated retopology workflows for human and animal character modeling in Blender.

---

## 1. Deformation Topology Flow Principles

Organic topology must mirror natural muscle fiber contraction lines and joint flexion:

```text
┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                      ORGANIC TOPOLOGY FLOW MAP                         │
├───────────────────┬────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ Facial Rings      │ Concentric quad loops around eyes (orbicularis     │
│                   │ oculi) and mouth (orbicularis oris)                │
├───────────────────┼────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ Joint Spans       │ 3-loop spans around bending joints (elbows, knees, │
│                   │ knuckles, hocks) to prevent volume collapse        │
├───────────────────┼────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ Torso & Ribcage   │ Diagonal loops contouring pectorals and latissimus │
│                   │ dorsi down to the pelvic crest                     │
├───────────────────┼────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ Animal Quadruped  │ Dedicated scapula (shoulder blade) slip loops and  │
│ Specifics         │ rear hock articulation loops for digitigrade legs  │
└───────────────────┴────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

### Prohibited Artifacts:
- **E-Poles (5-edge vertices) on Deforming Bends:** Never place 5-pole or 3-pole vertices directly on bending creases (e.g. inner elbow, eyelid margin). Move poles to stationary flat muscular planes.
- **Triangles on Silhouette Borders:** Keep all silhouette contours 100% quad-based.

